Is one of your file systems running low on SPACE (do a df)? Typically,
DUNIX's filesystem optimization is to take the least amount of TIME
possible to read/write data to disk, not caring as much about where it
places it, fragmentation of free space, etc. When a filesystem starts to
get full (around 80-90%), SPACE becomes more crucial, and the
optimization method is changed...

At last this is my observation on DUNIX and NetBSD (BSDism???).
