I have seen this when tapes have come in written in compressed mode,
and then trying to read them on a drive that did not support data
compression.  What drive type was the tape written on, and what are
you using to attempt to read the tapes.  The other thing to check is
the maximum block size your drive supports.  Not all drives will be
able to read very large block sizes.

