Subject: Tru64 UNIX V5.0 NFS interop problem
Date: 1999/08/25
Message-ID: <6cyaez8woj.fsf@rational.com>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 517320219
X-Us-Snail: Rational Software Corp., 20 Maguire Road, Lexington, MA  02421-3104
Sender: jtk@fructose
Organization: Rational Software Corporation
Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1

Tru64 UNIX V5.0 is slowly making its way to the streets (independent
software vendors have started getting copies).  Beware that its NFS V3
server cannot reliably handle clients which use read sizes >8192 bytes.
The problem seems data dependent--not all files fail to be readable.  It
affects both TCP and UDP mounts.

If you hit the bug, you'll see messages like this from the kernel:

Aug 25 10:26:59 durian vmunix: svckudp_send: xdr_replymsg failed
Aug 25 10:26:59 durian vmunix: rfs_dispatch: sendreply failed IP address: 172.21.150.222

Workaround:  use 8KB read/write sizes on your client mounts.  (For sites
like mine, though, this is unpalatable as it means I've got to set all
my clients up to use 8KB read/write for all the NFS servers since we use
automount -hosts maps.)
