This is a fairly common problem. It's in the D/T64 UNIX FAQ:

	M18. Why does dxaccounts tells me that the password and group
	files are locked?

	If a dxaccounts process exits ungracefully (e.g. if a kill -9 
	is used) then it sometimes leaves a file in /etc called
	.AM_is_running. Deleting this file will solve the problem.

                                        [Ian Lloyd]

Have fun!

Richard Moore wrote:
> 
> I have been having trouble adding/removing users.  The error that I get is
> 
> The password and group files are currently locked by another user.
> Please try again later.
> Error, exiting useradd /usr/sbin/adduser. Check /etc/passwd.
> 
> There is no one using these files.  I have downed the server and rebooted
> it, this didn't work.
> 
> Any Suggestions?
> Richard Moore
-- 

Until soon...
