Subject: Solved: Networker problem on 4.0F
Date: 1999/08/21
Message-ID: <6$ECc7NbxqE3@malvm2.mala.bc.ca>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 515546622
Organization: Malaspina University-College
Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1


   I posted a question here a couple of weeks ago about the license
for Networker expiring on  DUnix 4.0F.

   It appears the problem is that the "Networker" included in the
4.0F kit is not the "Single Server" edition (BRX kit) , but the
full blown Networker product (LGTO kit). The installation guide is
very confusing in this respect as it refers to a "BRX520" kit which
should be found on the Associated Products CD #2 in a
"Networker_SingleServer" directory, but neither the directory or that
kit exist , instead one finds a "Networker" directory which has a
"LGTO550" kit on it. I mistakenly installed this and it worked fine
until the 30 day evaluation license it creates upon installation expired.

   I fixed the problem by deleting this version of Networker and
installing the BRX440 kit which can be found in the DUnix 4.0D
distribution. Unfortunately it appears the media database and index
aren't backwards compatible, so I had to delete them as well
(not a major problem, but if I need to restore from an existing
tape I'll have to run scanner on it first ).

   The above posted in the hope it will prevent someone else from
getting similarly confused :-)

-- 
