BIOS?  Alpha?  Digital Unix?

Heh..  PC weenies.

Anyway, back to the original problem.  A frequent cause of Telnet session
start delays are due to the failure of the remote system to do a reverse name
lookup.  When the connection is made, the remote system tries to convert the
local system's IP address to a name, and it timed out after 2 minutes.

        Stu



