disk drive type. We have a "premium" service contract with DECompaq,
which means within a couple hours of calling in the problem, I have a
replacement part in my hands. They have not failed me yet with this
system (TZ8x drives on our OVMS systems are a different story).

If anything, I have been more worried about Compaq's support/strategy
with OpenVMS than I am when it comes to D/T64 UNIX. Whenever Compaq
publishes an article, it's about NT, T64 UNIX, and Linux. Whenever they
mention migration, it's always "FROM OpenVMS" and "TO NT/T64". To make
things more interesting, read the recent articles where Compaq is going
to drop development of NT on Alpha.

On the flip side, there's nothing that can be done about the Oracle
support. Keep in mind that OVMS updates are 90 days behind DUNIX
updates, which in turn are 90 days behind the rest. I realize it's all
about money, but you would think one of the big opponents of Microsoft
would be a little more enthusiastic when it came to supporting alternate
platforms, rather than just making a small handful their primary focus.

Dunno if that helps any, but there it is...
-- 
Until soon...
Ed Wensell III



