Hej.

acturro wrote:
> 
> does someone know how to send files selected i.e. by command find via
> ftp using automatic login information $HOME/.netrc? (as parameter list
> for command mput)
> 
> If pipe is on and the first character of the file name is the vertical
> bar (|) the remainder of the argument is interpreted as shell command.
> ftp then forks a shell.
> But it does not work.

Well, try this (you can write all this stuff on one line,
if you remove comments):

echo "machine <remote> login <yourname> password <yourpasswd> macdef init" >
.netrc;
echo "prompt" >> .netrc; # probably not needed
find . -name "whatever" -exec echo "put" {} >> .netrc \; ;
echo "bye" >> .netrc;
echo >> .netrc;
ftp;
rm -f .netrc # just in case (the file will be world readable, probably)

Change <remote> into your.remote.machine.name, <yourname> into your remote
login,
<yourpasswd> into your remote passwd, and <. -name "whatever"> into whatever you
use for your find command.

I'd install ssh and use scp in your case, however.

Regards,
Sua



