In article <7pemrm$5j7$1@nnrp1.deja.com> you wrote:

: This is an excerpt from the last uerf:
: tz12 at scsi1 target 4 lun 0 (LID=1)
: _(DEC     TZ87     (C) DEC 971B)
: tz13 at scsi1 target 5 lun 0 (LID=2)
: _(ARCHIVE Python 29279-XXX 499B)
: changer at scsi1 target 5 lun 1
: _(LID=3) (ARCHIVE Python 29279-XXX
: _499B)

: I haven't done a MAKEDEV yet as I'm not sure what args to give, eg,
: would I give tz13 as the arg to MAKEDEV?

Normally

cd /dev
ls *rmt*

the old/known ones are (n)rmtX*

X counter from 0 up to max_installed_drive

./MAKEDEV tzY     (Y your SCSI-ID)

because there are already installed devices so you will get
(n)rmt(X+1)*

If you want you may remove old ones (rm /dev/*rmt*) and install
only the new ones. But you should add the new one.

HTH 
        Juergen



