"Ga�l Trinquart" <gtrinquart@elan.fr> writes:

> I try to align 32-bit data (my system is 64-bit). The 32-bit alignement is
> properly done but the system outputs a runtime message "Unaligned access
> pid=8307 <syntz> va=1401b5294 pc=120071e8c ra=120071e24 type=stq".
> 
> I tried to close stdout and stderr but the message does not disappear. Any
> idea ?
> 
A few ideas:

1) Update your code so it is 64-bit aligned. This includes pointers, long
   integers, and doubles (long long).
2) Try compiling with the '-taso' flag; it forces the app to load in the
   lower 31-bit addressable virtual address range.  See the cc(1) man page
   for details.
3) Silence it with the 'uac' command, as in

      $ uac p noprint ; /run/the/unaligned/application -with options

   See the uac(1) man page for other options.

MarkG
