You should be able to get a list of commands by typing "help" at the
firmware prompt.  Sometimes the help isn't particularly helpful, since it
lists parameters but not the values they can hold.  In that case just type
the command without any parameters and hope the error it spits back lists
the valid parameters (sometimes it does).

You probably won't be able to do anything that's useful for a corrupted
filesystem from the firmware, though... more or less all you can do there
is "show dev" to confirm that the hard drive is showing up properly.

