skettle@my-deja.com wrote:

> When I try to link when building a binary I get unresolved references:
> eg.
>
> /usr/bin/ld:
> Unresolved:
> foo(int)
> bar(int*,int*)

> ...
> Is there any flag to ld that turns will prints out this type of info ?

See the linker's manpage "man ld" for the -y<sym> flag.  That flag
is position dependent so it needs to appear early in the link line so the
linker knows to search for the symbol <sym> in subsequent objects and
libraries.

Joe Mario





