dminor@salud.unm.edu wrote:
> 
> Hi. We had a box running 3.2c with several advfs vols on it. Yesterday
> we installed 4.0e on a new disk in the system and are in the process of
> migrating files, etc.

A risky job. Can this be actually done? Can you mount a 3.2-AdvFS on DU 4.0x? I
don't think so.

Also, note that there was a compatibilty bug between 4.0D and pre-4.0D AdvFS, so
mounting would cause system to crash.

> So far none of our advfs vols is showing up in the new setup. None of
> the advfs structure has changed. On boot you can see them scroll by with
> the message "no device." We did copy over the /etc/fdmns file which
> seems to be correct. Any suggestions?? This is kind of an emergency
> because all of our core stuff is on those vols.

When you installed 4.0E, were the old disks on? If not, then there are no
entries in /dev directory to access those disks/partitions. And
/etc/fdmns/<domain> has symbolic links to those files. Also, as stated above,
I'm not sure it can actually be done.

Try vdump/vrestore, it should be backwards compatible. Just to make it clear,
boot old DU 3.2, do vdump, boot 4.0E, do vrestore.

Nix.
-- 
