> 
> Hi. We had a box running 3.2c with several advfs vols on it. Yesterday
> we installed 4.0e on a new disk in the system and are in the process of
> migrating files, etc.
> 
> So far none of our advfs vols is showing up in the new setup. None of
> the advfs structure has changed. On boot you can see them scroll by with
> the message "no device." We did copy over the /etc/fdmns file which
> seems to be correct. Any suggestions?? This is kind of an emergency
> because all of our core stuff is on those vols.
> 
> TIA.
> 
> david.

I had a similar problem when moving an AdvFS from a V4.0B to V4.0D
system.
I believe DEC changed some of the internal details of AdvFS, which makes
the file systems unrecognised as AdvFS. If you do a standard upgrade,
the AdvFS get updated as well, so the problem only arises when moving
"old"
AdvFS onto new versions of D.U.
There may be a way to patch the AdvFS to be acceptable to V4.0E - but I 
just copied the disk contents (25GB I seem to recall :-( ) to tape,
moved 
the disks, reinitialised the AdvFS volumes and recovered from tape.

Regards,
John Hill



